{
	title: 'Approval reasons, env dumps and /help security',
	spec: "Each approval pattern has its own reason; the question shows each matched pattern's reason once, in match order, then the line '/help security to learn more.', above the marked command (no generic headline). Reasons: rm -rf: 'May wipe out important files by accident.' git reset --hard: 'Throws away uncommitted changes.' git clean: 'Wipes out untracked files for good.' git stash drop/clear: 'Throws away stashed changes.' git push --force: 'May clobber others' commits on the remote.' git checkout/restore of files: 'Throws away uncommitted changes in these files.' cat/head/tail of a sensitive path: 'Will likely leak your secrets.' Env dumps: 'Reveals env variables. If you have secrets like OPENAI_API_KEY in env, this will leak them.' Env dumps are ps with a dashed option group containing E (macOS), ps whose first argument is a BSD option group containing e, and any /proc/<pid>/environ path, which the sensitive-path policy (READ, snapshots) also covers. Public keys (*.pub) are never sensitive, even under .ssh/. /help accepts topics after commands; tab completion offers them and the full list ends with a Topics line. The security topic says what Hal asks about, which files count as secret, where a leaked secret goes (sent to the provider, stored in plaintext in session files), that it stops mistakes rather than a determined attacker such as a man-in-the-middle at the provider, and points to /config security.",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'ps -e is all processes on both macOS and Linux, not env; only -E (dashed) and e (undashed, first argument) show env. The undashed check looks only at the first argument so -o user is not taken for an e group.',
		'Keys seen in ps -E (user report): only Hal and its children carried OPENAI_API_KEY; login, zsh and ./run did not. The source of the key in bun is not yet known.',
		"The no-approval security value is 'yolo' (was 'none'); an old 'none' in the config is invalid and falls back to best-effort, by the user's choice. Approval questions are titled 'Approval needed'; a question's title is its text's first line, the rest is body text in the body color, in both clients (forms.title, forms.details)."
	],
